# Fully Featured Banking System

A fully functional console-based banking system built in Java. It includes secure user authentication, account and transaction management, and persistent storage using a relational database. The application follows object-oriented design principles and a modular architecture for maintainability and scalability.
## Overview

This project simulates a simple banking system supporting multiple users, each with one or more bank accounts. Users can perform deposits, withdrawals, and transfers. All actions are logged in transaction history and persisted in a database.

## Features

- User Authentication
  - Registration and login system
  - Password hashing with salt for security

- Account Management
  - Support for multiple accounts per user
  - Account type, ID, and balance stored in the database

- Transaction Management
  - Deposit, withdraw, and transfer funds
  - Transaction history with timestamps

- Testing
  - Unit tests for core logic and services
  - Integration tests for database operations

- Modular Design
  - Uses interfaces and separation of concerns
  - Follows SOLID principles

- Database Integration
  - JDBC-based connection to MySQL
  - Data persistence for users, accounts, and transactions

## Technologies Used

- Java 17
- JDBC
- MySQL
- JUnit
- Git and GitHub
- No Maven/Gradle needed

